Source: beacond
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: beacond maintainers <beacond@example.com>
# Go >= 1.22 must be on PATH at build time (see go.mod). It is intentionally
# NOT expressed as a Build-Depends: Debian stable's golang-go can lag behind
# the go.mod floor (e.g. bookworm ships 1.19), so builds use an upstream Go
# toolchain instead (the golang:<ver>-bookworm image, or a manually installed
# one). go.mod's `go 1.22` is the real floor; `go build` fails loudly on an
# older toolchain rather than silently misbuilding.
#
# debhelper (>= 13.6~) is required because debian/rules explicitly invokes
# dh_installsysusers (added in debhelper 13.6); the bare compat-13 pin alone
# is satisfied by older debhelper (e.g. 13.3 on Debian 11 bullseye), where
# that helper does not exist yet.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), debhelper (>= 13.6~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/example/beacond
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: beacond
# ${shlibs:Depends} always resolves empty here (CGO_ENABLED=0 -> no dynamic
# library dependencies to discover) and dpkg-gencontrol warns "substitution
# variable ${shlibs:Depends} used, but is not defined" on every build.
# That's expected for a static Go binary, not a sign anything is wrong;
# ${shlibs:Depends} is kept anyway so this Depends: line does not need a
# manual audit if CGO or a dynamically-linked dependency is ever
# introduced. ${misc:Depends} is doing real work below: dh_installsysusers
# expands it to "systemd | systemd-standalone-sysusers | systemd-sysusers"
# automatically (verified against the built package), which is the only
# place that dependency comes from -- there is no explicit `Depends:
# systemd` in this file.
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: small heartbeat daemon
 beacond is a small, dependency-free heartbeat daemon. It reads a tiny config
 file, listens on a TCP address (a loopback port by default, so it needs no
 elevated capabilities), and answers /health with a JSON status and the
 running build version.
 .
 This package installs the beacond binary, its systemd service, the
 /etc/beacond/beacond.yaml config, and creates the dedicated beacon system
 user under which it runs. The service works out of the box: the packaged
 config already matches the daemon's built-in defaults.

Package: beacond-client
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, curl
Description: status client for beacond
 beacon-status is a small, architecture-independent bash client that queries
 a beacond instance's /health endpoint and reports whether it answered.
 .
 This package does not depend on beacond itself: it only needs network
 access to a beacond endpoint, which is commonly a different host. It also
 installs /etc/profile.d/beacon-env.sh, which sets the default
 BEACON_ENDPOINT for interactive login shells.
